  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "COMPLEX formats coefficients to 15 digits via directed x87 rounding, turns DBL_MIN into \"0\", and rejects DBL_MAX",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20430 and 20527, COMPLEX(real_num, i_num, [suffix]) formats each nonzero coefficient to 15 significant digits via ExactDecimal::fifteen_x87 (floor(frexp_k / 3.3219), nibble-chain scaling, exact half-up ties, and 16-digit binary64 half-down re-scale on k = -485, -970 slivers), using fixed notation up to 21 unsigned characters and scientific notation beyond. It rejects exact DBL_MAX (0x7fefffffffffffff) with #NUM!, emits \"0\" (\"0i\") when rounding DBL_MIN to 15 digits falls below DBL_MIN, omits unit imaginary coefficients (\"i\", \"-i\"), and accepts only \"\", \"i\", or \"j\" as suffix (#VALUE! otherwise). All 10,709 full-bank COMPLEX rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
